coth0205	Kevin: But the new special edition has point-and-click--
coth0206	Bret: I just found that out today.
coth0207	Kevin: You can play it as was imagined, the boundary-pushing experiment, or you can--
coth0208	Bret: They have erased all our innovation!
coth0209	Kevin: Or you can play it the right way.
coth0210	Bret: Thank God our innovation has been undone.
coth0211	Kevin: Yes. We don't need that crap anymore.
coth0301	Tim: There is no-- This is a really boring fact, I'm going to share it anyway. There is no inventory combinations in "Grim Fandango." You can't use an object with another object in your inventory.
coth0302	Peter M: Oh, that's right.
coth0303	Tim: So if you wanna put the bone in the bone grinder, you have to put them in this receptacle in the room. Another weird mechanical contrivance from my own head: a handheld snow grinder that would plug into a giant snow grinder. I'm sure they have those, right?
coth0304	Peter M: What's a snow grinder?
coth0305	Tim: It's like a fake, like, to make fake snow for the show. And this is what I was talking about, you can't use the hand with the snow grinder.
