tmpts01	Hey!  Shut door!  You slow down my grinder, very painful!  Very painful, eh Naranja?  Like torture, Hehehe...hehe?
tmpts02	Shut the damn door!  Nothing to eat in there!  You will want a snack, go get mother!
tmpts03	Stay out of my fridge!  [Don't make me come in there and kick your ass!]
tmpts04	I kill you!
tmpts05	Eh?  Who is over there?
tmpts06	[What the hell?]  Look!  You broke it.
tmpts07	Now it won't shut.
tmpts08	When I am done with Naranja here, I am going to tattoo big, floppy ears on the side of your head so people will know what a jackass you are!
tmpts09	(busy, dismissive grunt)
tmpts10	Argh. Not now, Manny.  I'm in the middle of something with Naranja here.
tmpts11	I told you Calavera, not now.
tmpts13	You push me to edge, Calavera!
tmpts14	Why are you down here, anyway?
tmpts15	Ah, get lost!
tmpts16	Don't you have some fancy club to run someplace?
tmpts17	Go mark some cards or something.
tmpts18	Shut up!
tmpts19	Yeah, I got to remember to get more liquid nitrogen from morgue.
tmpts20	Freeze the bones, less painful that way.
tmpts21	You got plenty of pain killer in that bottle of yours, so shut up and hold still!
tmpts22	I kill the pain.  Turn off my drill, stop working.  How about that?
tmpts23	I'll 'pop' you, sailor-boy...
tmpts24	You need to hold still, or I need to strap you down.
tmpts25	Put that crazy blade away.  No room in here for that kind of thing!
tmpts26	What is that?  Am I being inspected?  Are you with the health department or something?  Go away.  I pay my money this month.
tmpts27	Not impressed.
tmpts28	Too big -- Take off the whole arm.  Only do that if design turns out bad.
tmpts29	Ha!  Communism is dead!
tmpts30	But at least there was a time when "I" worked!  Eh?  Ha ha ha!
tmpts31	What?  Are you trying to sell me something?
tmpts32	Hmmm.  I haven't had a good piece of Lengua since you shut Rub-A-Mat down!  (sigh)  You and your fancy food, (muttering off) with the parsley and the foil swans...
tmpts33	Manny, do you mind?  Artist at work here, eh?
tmpts34	Oh yeah, yeah, yeah.  That is what I told him.
tmpts35	Are you kidding me?
tmpts36	I gave him the idea in first place!
tmpts37	Ah, tiger can't change his stripes.
tmpts38	So you still going to go?
tmpts39	Hey, listen to me--you've got to take care of yourself.
tmpts40	Yeah. Yeah, yeah. Yeah.
tmpts41	Uh-huh. Uh-huh. Uh-huh.
tmpts42	Sure.
tmpts43	Sure, of course.  I understand.
tmpts44	Definitely.
tmpts45	Mmmm-hmmmm. Mmmm-hmmm.
tmpts46	You said that?
tmpts47	You've got guts!
tmpts48	Yeah, but I wouldn't exactly call that 'quality time.'
tmpts49	So, what happened after dinner?
tmpts50	Ah-ha. Ah-ha.
tmpts51	Oh, you're kidding me!
tmpts52	Oh, I don't believe it.
tmpts53	What about kids?
tmpts54	That is just crying shame.
tmpts55	MMMMM...
tmpts56	Well, if you didn't tell me someone else would.
tmpts57	I'd tell you, but I cannot.
tmpts58	Someone else is here.
tmpts59	Let's just say it is bad.
tmpts60	Yes. Yes. Tears were shed.
tmpts61	No, no, go...go ahead.  Tell me the whole thing.  I am listening.
tmpts62	Uh, hang on second.
tmpts63	AH AH AH!  Get away from that!
tmpts64	No, no!  What are you thinking?
tmpts65	Reach for that again, and you will pull back a stump!
tmpts66	You mean, besides the song, and the poem, and the bar, and the statue by that name?
tmpts67	Sure!  It is one of my most famous designs!  Here, I show you!
tmpts68	Let's see... uh, number thirty... ah, thirty-six.  Here. Hey... what is this?
tmpts69	Kissy people?
tmpts70	Oh, oh, yeah.  Lola was here.  Sweet girl.  Like daughter to me.  Tell her Papa Toto say hello.
tmpts71	Zzzzzzzz.
tmpts72	Zzzzzzzz.
tmpts73	Zzzzzzzz.
tmpts74	...Hold still...
tmpts75	...stop moving...
tmpts76	...color cost more...
tmpts77	...doesn't hurt...
tmpts78	...quit whining...
tmpts79	...shut your hole...
tmpts80	...I kill you...
tmpts81	...I "am"... I "am" an artist...
tmpts82	...you "asked" for bunny...
tmpts83	...not my fault...
tmpts84	...your mother will love it...
tmpts85	...Lola...
tmpma01	Hola, Toto. ¿Cómo estás?
tmpma02	What's that you're working on there?
tmpma03	Caterpillar?
tmpma04	A mouse?
tmpma05	A caterpillar eating a mouse?
tmpma06	Is that a shoe?
tmpma07	Is that supposed to be a bunny?
tmpma08	Looks good, whatever it is.
tmpma09	I think that art class has really helped.
tmpma10	Keep up the good work.
tmpma11	Can I try it for a while?
tmpma12	Missed a spot.
tmpma13	I can't really make it out, but it looks like my parents fighting.
tmpma14	I think I hear you grinding your teeth.  You really shouldn't do that.
tmpma15	I'm thinking about heading out for donuts.  Want anything?
tmpma16	It's a little cabinet.
tmpma17	It's empty.
tmpma18	Liquid nitrogen?
tmpma19	Strong stuff.  That oughta kill the pain.
tmpma20	That's one old fridge.
tmpma21	Nothin' in there but stains.
tmpma22	Looks like a lettuce crisper.
tmpma23	..."smells" more like a "fungus" crisper to me, though.
tmpma24	Lot of stains for a guy with no bodily fluids.
tmpma25	I really doubt I'll be touching that any time soon.
tmpma26	Oooh, that reminds me.  I forgot about my date with Inez!
tmpma27	Hello, operator?
tmpma28	Yeah, it's me baby.  How'd you know?
tmpma29	Hey, don't say that sweetheart.  You know I meant to stop by--
tmpma30	I'm more happy about leaving town every minute.
tmpma31	I think I'll stay off the phone for a while.  Just until Inez calms down.
tmpma32	Doesn't look like YOU'LL be showing up to work in the morning.
tmpma33	Let's see what you got on ya sailor.
tmpma34	Hmmm...
tmpma35	Seaman Anselmo Naranja.  Ensign, third class.
tmpma36	So are we.
tmpma37	Never get "me" under that thing.
tmpma38	This mean anything to you?
tmpma39	Yes.
tmpma40	My friend Lola left that here for me.
tmpma41	Sure thing.
syma218	I'm sick of waiting around for a good lead, like it's going to fly in here tied to a brick. 
syma219	It's time to TAKE one. 
	
